Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:55:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 29/37] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: Share the camera, add J714c,
 J716s, K114s, K116c

The T6050 camera (ISP, its three DARTs and its power states) was
described for J714s, J716c and K116s only, in t6050-j716c-isp.dtsi.
Nothing in that file is J716c specific: each laptop's ADT has the same
isp0, dart-isp0 and ISP power states (registers, interrupts, streams,
power-state offsets). The only per-board value is the isp0 sensor-type,
and the boot loader reads that from the ADT and passes it on as the
platform ID.

Rename the file to t6050-isp.dtsi and include it from J714c, J716s,
K114s and K116c as well. Each board's include notes its sensor-type
from that board's ADT. Every node stays disabled until the loader has
reserved the camera firmware, so a loader without a row for the board
leaves the camera off.

The J714s, J716c and K116s DTBs are byte-identical. K114c is left out
here: its camera is described in a separate open change. J775c, J775d
and J873s have no camera and are unchanged.

The original J716c description is by Erik Bourget.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
